      en: "Saint Joseph Church in Bangui was built in 1936 by French missionaries. It is one of the oldest churches in the country and an example of colonial architecture with Neo-Romanesque elements. The church has a massive bell tower and colorful stained glass windows depicting biblical scenes. It serves as the cathedral for the Archdiocese of Bangui. In recent years, the church has been renovated. It is an important religious and cultural center, with regular masses and community events.",
