      en: "The Central African National Library in Bangui was founded in 1986 and is the largest library in the country. It houses a collection of over 50,000 books, including rare historical works and manuscripts. The library plays an important role in preserving national heritage and promoting reading. Due to limited resources, the collection is not fully cataloged. The library offers a reading room and occasional cultural events. It is an important educational site in the capital.",
